Z||000000||Greg Piet||03-03-2001||11:31 PM||||Uhhh this JUST happened so I am a bit concerned (during normal city driving).<BR>1985 v6 with 4 speed<BR>My clutch used to be really really stiff (hard to depress) compared to all the other clutches I have used.<BR>Now all of a sudden it got very easy to depress (like most other cars for example 85 Rx7 and 97 Toyota P/U I JUST compared to).  The radio was on when it happened so I didnt hear a THWOING or something of that nature.  The car is operating, but I have yet to see if the clutch is slipping.  <BR>Anyone else have this experience?  Are others clutches really hard to depress?  If you have expereinced this what was the problem.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">  <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||9
Z||000001||Greg Piet||03-04-2001||05:38 PM||||Ok she is slipping on the launch, so I am guessing the clutch is gone.  I dont know how many miles are on the clutch, but it had a year of hard driving, including 3000 miles of towing a VW buggy.  Looking at the Fierostore Kevlar clutch...  any comments? ||||reg||1
